9	How to become an IRS-approved
10	accreditor to approve continuing
11	education providers
12	
13	  More In Tax Pros                                                                          +
14	
15	
16	
17	Review Revenue Procedure 2012-12, which describes the procedures and standards that
18	organizations must follow to be identified by the Internal Revenue Service as a qualifying
19	organization that may accredit continuing education providers under section 10.9(a)(1)(iii)
20	of Circular 230 PDF .
21	
22	
23	Application must include the organization's:
24	   Full name
25	   Mailing address
26	   Telephone number
27	   Web address (URL)
28	   Tax identification number
29	   Point of contact
30	       Mailing address
31	       Telephone number
32	       Email address
33	
34	   Requirements an individual or entity must meet to obtain your organization's approval
35	   as a CE provider.
36	       Attach supporting documentation for the requirements.
37	
38	   Experience and qualifications evaluating CE providers.
39	   Process to review applications from CE providers, showing compliance with Circular 230
40	   standards.
41	       Attach supporting documentation of the process.
42	
43	   Statement that it won't directly or indirectly oﬀer commercial continuing education in
44	   federal tax matters or ethics during any period that the organization is operating as an
45	   accrediting organization.
46	   Statement that it agrees to comply with all IRS guidance and requirements, including
47	   Circular 230.
48	   Statement that it acknowledges that its status as an IRS accrediting organization is
49	   subject to review at any time by the IRS, including but not limited to:
50	       IRS requests for information about the organization's review and approval process,
51	       interviews, and site visitations (including site visitations of the organization's
52	       approved CE providers).
53	       That the organization's failure to provide any data or information requested by the
54	       IRS or its denial of an IRS site visitation may result in suspension or revocation of its
55	       accrediting organization status.
56	
57	   Signed and dated statement by its point of contact, oﬀicer, partner, member or owner
58	   providing that the individual has examined and read the application and all
59	   accompanying information and to the best of the individual's knowledge and belief, the
60	   information provided is true, correct and complete. For example:
61	
62	Under penalty of perjury, I declare that I have examined this application and read all
63	accompanying information, and to the best of my knowledge and belief, the information
64	provided is true, correct and complete. I understand any false or misleading information
65	may result in criminal penalties and/or the denial or revocation of my (our) status as an IRS
66	accreditor of CE providers.
67	
68	
69	How and where to submit application
70	   The statements can be on one page, along with the jurat and signature
71	   Mailing address
72	
73	Internal Revenue Service
74	Attn: RPO Continuing Education Program
75	1122 Town and Country Commons
76	Chesterfield, MO 63017
77	
78	
79	What to expect
80	   IRS will notify applicants in writing of approval within 21 days of receiving the
81	   completed application.
82	   Once approved, the online CE provider system will recognize CE providers as accredited.
